BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Expert Panels: 2026 Art & Design Graduate School Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T153000
UID:expert-panels-2026-art-design-graduate-school-fair@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Have questions about graduate school? Join us on October 7 for
  our Expert Panel series! This series includes two panels that will cover 
 a variety of topics to help support you in your graduate school journey.\n
 \nExpert Panels: Art & Design Graduate School Fair Date: Wednesday\, Octob
 er 7\, 2026 Location: CEAD\, 115 McCaul St.\, 3rd Floor Full Details here 
 Have questions about graduate school? Join us on October 7 for our Expert 
 Panel series! This series includes two panels that will cover a variety of
  topics to help support you in your graduate school journey. Schedule of e
 vents: How Graduate School Shapes Creative Practice - 1:00 p.m. - 2:00 p.m
 . - RSVP to attend What happens when you take your creative practice beyon
 d an undergraduate degree? Join a panel of artists and designers who will 
 reflect on their graduate school experiences and discuss how pursuing an M
 FA or MDes helped shape their creative identities\, research interests\, a
 nd professional careers. Whether you're considering graduate studies now o
 r exploring future possibilities\, this conversation will offer honest ins
 ights\, practical advice\, and inspiration to help you determine if gradua
 te school is the right path for you. Panelists: - Natia Lemay (MFA) - Chia
 ra Garrido (MDes) - Camilo Rodriguez (MFA) - Maryem Abbas (MDes) The Gradu
 ate School Application Toolkit - 2:30 p.m. - 3:30 p.m. - RSVP to attend Pr
 eparing for graduate school can be overwhelming\, but knowing what admissi
 ons teams are looking for can make all the difference. Join graduate recru
 itment and admissions professionals as they share expert guidance on craft
 ing compelling application materials\, including your CV\, portfolio\, and
  statement of intent. Learn common mistakes to avoid\, strategies for high
 lighting your strengths\, and tips for creating a cohesive application tha
 t reflects your creative and academic goals. Panelists: - California Insti
 tute of the Arts (CalArts) - Emily Carr University of Art + Design - Unive
 rsity of Toronto - John H. Daniels Faculty of Architecture\, Landscape\, a
 nd Design - Concordia University - OCAD University The panels will be foll
 owed by the Graduate School Fair the next day on October 8th from 11 a.m. 
 - 3 p.m . Art & Design Graduate School Fair Date/Time: Thursday\, October 
 8\, 2026\, from 11:00 am – 3:00 pm Location: 100 McCaul St. - OCAD Unive
 rsity\, Great Hall\, 2nd Floor RSVP to attend “Which schools will be the
 re?” University of the Arts London\, Emily Carr University of Art & Desi
 gn\, California Institute of the Arts\, plus many more ! Are you consideri
 ng graduate-level studies? Join us on October 8th for the annual Art & Des
 ign Graduate School Fair at OCAD University to meet with representatives f
 rom top art & design universities\, including OCAD University\, to learn m
 ore about MFA\, MDes\, MA\, and PhD programs throughout Canada or internat
 ionally.
LOCATION:Rosalie Sharp Pavillion (MCD) 115 McCaul St. Level 3
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/gradschoolfair
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
